## **1. Definitions**

This License refers to version 1 of The Nae's Public License.

Copyleft means the condition under which the use, modification, or distribution of the Software is permitted only if any resulting work is licensed in its entirety under this License.

Software means the source code, compiled binaries, documentation, assets, and all associated materials provided under this License.

Source Code means the preferred form of the Software for making modifications, including all files necessary to build, install, run, and modify the Software.

Complete Corresponding Source Code means all source code, build scripts, configuration files, and environmental requirements necessary to reproduce the exact functionality of the Software. This includes any modified libraries, dependencies, or wrapper components not readily accessible to the general public. Only unmodified system libraries that are publicly accessible without cost, registration, or restriction may be excluded.

Derivative Work means any work that copies from or adapts all or part of the Software in a manner requiring permission under applicable copyright law, other than the making of an exact copy.

Distribution means making the Software or a Derivative Work available to any third party.

Service Use means providing the functionality of the Software or a Derivative Work to users over a network, including but not limited to software-as-a-service (SaaS), APIs, or hosted environments.

Commercial Activity means any activity intended for monetary gain, including but not limited to sales, subscriptions, or advertising-supported services.

**Third-Party Content** means any data, content, or material that is not part of the Software or a Derivative Work, including but not limited to data retrieved from external systems, user-provided input, or network resources.

The mere retrieval, transmission, processing, or rendering of Third-Party Content by the Software does not cause such content to become part of the Software or a Derivative Work.

