## **6. No Paywall or Access Restriction**

The Software, in both Source Code and compiled form, must be freely obtainable without payment or any required exchange of value.

Charging for hosting infrastructure, operational services, or human support is permitted, provided that access to the Software itself remains unrestricted and free of charge.

---

## **7. Advertising Prohibition**

The Software and any Derivative Work must not include, implement, or intentionally facilitate the display of advertising.

For the purposes of this License, advertising includes any content, message, or material intended to promote products, services, or brands.

Functionality whose primary purpose is to retrieve, inject, prioritize, or render advertising content shall be considered part of the Software.

The Software shall not be considered in violation of this section solely for displaying or transmitting Third-Party Content that contains advertising, provided that:

a. The advertising content is not introduced, modified, or selectively prioritized by the Software; and
b. The Software does not include functionality specifically designed to enable, enhance, or optimize the delivery of such advertising.

Any intentional integration of advertising systems, including but not limited to ad networks, tracking-based ad delivery, or sponsored content injection, constitutes a violation of this License.

For the avoidance of doubt, Third-Party Content displayed or transmitted without modification or selective prioritization shall not be considered part of the Software.

---

## **8. Privacy and Data Collection**

The Software shall not include any mechanism for tracking, profiling, or collecting user data except as expressly permitted below:

a. Minimal telemetry may be collected solely for aggregate usage measurement. Such telemetry must not identify, track, or profile individual users or devices across sessions, and must not include persistent identifiers or correlation mechanisms.

b. Crash reporting is permitted only with explicit, per-incident user consent and must be limited strictly to information necessary for technical error diagnosis.

Any data collection beyond the foregoing constitutes a material breach of this License.

